<speak>Electronic copies are generally sufficient. I print something when I intend to spend time reading it, not because I want a permanent paper archive of everything. There are already too many folders in the study. Some are from the business and should have gone back to the office long ago. I am slowly sorting them, but I do not want that to become my new occupation. The cabinet restoration is a more appealing reason to spend time in this room than sorting old correspondence.</speak>